Subject: [PATCH] build: enable the AAC (ADTS) parser

The existing --disable-everything configuration enables AAC decoding and the
MPEG-TS/HLS demuxers, but not the aac parser. FFmpeg's MPEG-TS demuxer asks
for full parsing of every PES stream, ff_read_packet() then finds no parser
for AAC and silently degrades the stream to AVSTREAM_PARSE_NONE. Each PES
packet, which may hold several ADTS frames, then receives the duration of a
single codec frame (1024 samples, 21.3 ms at 48 kHz) instead of its real span.
WineDMO credits that under-reported duration to its buffering accounting, so
HLS audio under-credits its queued read-ahead and false-starves.

Enable the upstream ADTS parser. It splits each PES into single frames with
correct timestamps and durations. Do not change WineDMO, its buffering
accounting or any timestamp to conceal the fault. This also changes packet
granularity for AAC streams from every demuxer that requests parsing and needs
runtime qualification; it is not a validated fix merely because the patch
applies.

Apply to the GE superproject after the crypto and MPEGVIDEO build patches
(its context includes the MPEGVIDEO flag). Requires fresh pin provenance and a
new whole-file Makefile.in postimage. No existing candidate pin or prepared
tree may be updated in place. Project-authored build integration, not an
upstream GE patch.
---
diff --git a/Makefile.in b/Makefile.in
--- a/Makefile.in
+++ b/Makefile.in
@@ -365,6 +365,7 @@
 	--enable-bsfs \
 	--disable-decoder=vvc \
 	--enable-parser=mpegvideo \
+	--enable-parser=aac \
 
 FFMPEG_i386-unix_CONFIGURE_ARGS := \
 	--cross-prefix=i686-linux-gnu- \
